    620  f24e							; LaserWallClamp $F25A (name+pin kept — sim_frame_budget beam_cols keys on
    621  f24e							; the entry; redesign 2026-10-08): CONTACT wall test — tests ONLY the
    622  f24e							; missile TIP cell (one display col x band rows RoomY+2..3) instead of
    623  f24e							; walking the whole swept path. The sweep/phase machine is gone: bank0
    624  f24e							; LaserInput now travels LaserX +/-4px/frame from the eye, capped at the
    625  f24e							; old sweep extent (RoomX+20 / max(RoomX-20,0)) and resets on contact, so
    626  f24e							; there is no path to clamp and CollisionX is never modified (old S6
    627  f24e							; mid-wall tip clamp retired with the sweep).
    628  f24e							; In (bank0 LaserInput .LaserGo): CollisionX = LaserX, drawn M0 = [A-7,A],
    629  f24e							; PlayerDir live, RoomY live, PF0Buf = the render map (bomb holes = air),
    630  f24e							; patch-strip marker = LineCount x OvHead/OvTail (LWpSetup, $F600).
    631  f24e							; M1 patch strip: tip px in [M1X-7, M1X] (M1X = (RoomPF0Lo)+14) = solid
    632  f24e							; A=2 — the mirror walk alone passes the cell (patch = open, envelope) and
    633  f24e							; the beam used to sail through the async block; kill-aware (b4 skip).
    634  f24e							;   right: tip px = A	      left: tip px = A-7 (A < 7 -> off-screen ->
    635  f24e							;     clear -> enemy loop, no wall)
    636  f24e							; Results: solid -> A=2 wall contact via ReturnPad (caller resets the beam
    637  f24e							; to the eye); clear -> jmp LaserClampDone = enemy loop (0/$50/1).
    638  f24e							; Entered/exited via jmp from/to LaserHitTestBody — stack depth unchanged
    639  f24e							; (SP guard: gameplay >= $F8; laser chain = 2 jsr from overscan = $FB).
    640  f24e							; Clobbers A/X/Y/RectCount/FetchPtr + CollisionEndX (marker scratch only).
    641  f24e							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
